.TH CHERUBSHRC 5 "August 2026" "CherubSH" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
cherubshrc \- interactive CherubSH startup file
.SH DESCRIPTION
An interactive, non-login CherubSH shell reads
.I ~/.cherubrc
unless startup options select another path or disable the file. CherubSH does
not use
.I ~/.bashrc
as a fallback.
.PP
Use
.B --norc
to skip the file. Use
.B --rcfile
or
.B --init-file
with a path to read another file.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
export EDITOR="${EDITOR:-vi}"
set -o vi
alias ll='ls -alF'

if [[ -r /usr/share/bash-completion/bash_completion ]]; then
    source /usr/share/bash-completion/bash_completion
fi
.fi
.SH LOGIN AND OTHER MODES
Login shells use the supported Bash-style profile sequence. Non-interactive
shells may read the file named by BASH_ENV. POSIX and sh-compatible interactive
modes may read the file named by ENV.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cherubrc
Default interactive, non-login startup file.
.TP
.I /etc/profile
System login profile.
.TP
.IR ~/.bash_profile , " " ~/.bash_login , " " ~/.profile
User login profiles, checked in that order when the current mode permits them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cherubsh (1)
